From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:22:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: write the HDMI
 converter power the ADT way

The J604's HDMI port runs through a DP-to-HDMI converter powered by two
SMC outputs, gP0f (hdmi_pwr_en) and gP1a (dp2hdmi_pwr_en). The ADT's
dp2hdmi functions write them as pKW4("gP0f", 0x00800000) and
pKW4("gP1a", 0x0): a fixed template with the level in the low bits.
macsmc-gpio writes its generic output command instead unless the board
names a template (apple,output-templates).

Name both templates, so turning the converter on writes what macOS
writes.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index d881f50ca0..218f91d7c4 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -1796,3 +1796,13 @@ ramoops@10200000000 {
 &cluster_pwrgate {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * The HDMI converter's two power outputs, written as the ADT's dp2hdmi
+ * functions do: hdmi_pwr_en = pKW4("gP0f", 0x00800000) and dp2hdmi_pwr_en =
+ * pKW4("gP1a", 0x0), the level in the low bits, not the generic output
+ * command.
+ */
+&smc_gpio {
+	apple,output-templates = <0x0f 0x00800000>, <0x1a 0x00000000>;
+};
